From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: use the exact rate for refresh-only requests

Steam's refresh rate slider asks for a rate with ONLY_CHANGE_REFRESH_RATE,
but the rate is still picked by refresh doubling: the highest supported rate
that is a multiple of the request. On a panel with only 60 and 120 Hz, 60
becomes 120. Use the requested rate when the connector supports it. Frame
limit requests keep doubling.

---
diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index 373d697..1f9f0d3 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -1290,6 +1290,14 @@ static void _update_app_target_refresh_cycle()
 	{
 		auto rates = GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetValidDynamicRefreshRates();
 
+		// A refresh-only request names a rate, not a frame cap: don't double it.
+		if ( !g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeFPS[ type ] &&
+			std::find( rates.begin(), rates.end(), uint32_t( target_fps ) ) != rates.end() )
+		{
+			g_nDynamicRefreshRate[ type ] = target_fps;
+			return;
+		}
+
 		// Find highest mode to do refresh doubling with.
 		for ( auto rate = rates.rbegin(); rate != rates.rend(); rate++ )
 		{
